Claim 1 (CPU): Linux x86-64, Python 3.12, Git, uv, 2 CPU cores, 2 GB RAM,
and about 4 GB free disk. Docker and a GPU are not needed.

Claim 2 (GPU): Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.34 or newer; an NVIDIA GPU with
compute capability 8.0 or newer and at least 24 GB VRAM; NVIDIA driver
575.51.03 or newer; Bash, Git, uv, rootful Docker, jq, and curl. We recommend
8 CPU cores, 32 GB RAM, and 80 GB free disk.

Both claims need network access for the initial downloads, and Claim 2 also
for image builds. No GUI, paid service, or API key is required. Claim 2
starts a privileged Docker-in-Docker container for scenario 06, so run it on
an isolated host. TCP port 5000 must be free on the Docker host for the local
image cache.

Public infrastructure: Claim 1 runs on any Linux VM. Bare-metal nodes on
Chameleon or CloudLab, or cloud GPU VMs, that meet the Claim 2 requirements
above can run Claim 2.
